      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "“Although system dynamics modeling has been utilized in various aspects of public health since the 1970s, past reviews in this field have noted a significant increase in their use since the early 2000s, especially in areas focused on chronic or non-communicable diseases [24, 25]. The extent to which system dynamics modeling has been applied specifically to cancer prevention and control has not been studied.”",
      "reason": "The introduction describes the current state of knowledge (system dynamics used in public health and increasing use) and notes an important gap/uncertainty (“has not been studied” for cancer prevention and control), but it does not clearly describe other uncertainties about the topic beyond this application gap."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "“Standard bench and clinical research approaches alone are not well suited to account for this complexity, as most cancer control interventions often focus on explicit, often linear health outcomes of a specific, well-defined population [1, 8, 9]. To overcome persistent barriers to providing high-quality, equitable care, approaches are needed to address this complexity and provide guidance for successful intervention.”",
      "reason": "It explains why a review is needed by stating existing approaches are insufficient for cancer’s complexity and that approaches are required to overcome barriers and guide successful intervention."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not explain the need for the current review in light of similar systematic reviews, nor does it identify/cite previous systematic reviews as updates/replications."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not describe this review as an evaluation of intervention effects, so the conditional requirement to briefly describe a proposed mechanism of action of an intervention is not applicable based on the available text."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not indicate the review is about complex interventions/delivery contexts in a way that would require a logic model; therefore this conditional requirement is not applicable based on the available information."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 62
}

{
