      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Cancer prevention and control requires consideration of complex interactions between multilevel factors. System dynamics modeling, which consists of diagramming and simulation approaches for understanding and managing such complexity, is being increasingly applied to cancer prevention and control, but the breadth, characteristics, and quality of these studies is not known.",
      "reason": "The review’s aim/intent is described (to address unknown breadth/characteristics/quality), but an explicit, structured statement of review objectives or question(s) using a relevant question-formulation framework is not clearly provided in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "The study was not registered in the International Prospective Register of Systematic Reviews (PROSPERO) as it was a methods review and did not assess health outcomes.",
      "reason": "No planned intervention-effect comparisons (e.g., PICO) are described because the review is a methods review that does not assess health outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 62
}

